// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO22 - internal power-gate for the onboard
// NeoPixel (RGB_PWR), not general-purpose.
//
// pfodWeb NOTE: button/LED capability-tagging audit, 2026-07-12.
// Board: Unexpected Maker TinyC6 (ESP32-C6). Dedicated-hardware
// pin-exclusion audit (GPIO22 above) was done in an earlier pass; this
// pass adds the section-7a button/LED tags that pass never applied.
//
// Virtual-pin resolution: pins_arduino.h declares
// "#define RGB_BUILTIN (RGB_DATA + SOC_GPIO_PIN_COUNT)" with
// "static const uint8_t RGB_DATA = 23;" - RGB_BUILTIN itself is a virtual
// pin number (SOC_GPIO_PIN_COUNT + 23) that build_boards.js's regex
// parser cannot resolve, so the real onboard GPIO tagged below is 23
// (RGB_DATA), not the RGB_BUILTIN virtual value.
//
// Source consulted (authoritative, vendor's own KiCad schematic):
// https://github.com/UnexpectedMaker/esp32c6/raw/main/TinyC6/TinyC6_Schematic_P1.pdf
// (TinyC6_P1.kicad_sch, Rev P1, 2023-11-18). The "RGB LED" schematic
// block shows LED2 (WS2812B1515) with DI wired to IO23 and VDD wired
// through IO22 (RGB_PWR power-gate, already excluded above) - confirms
// GPIO23 is the real WS2812/NeoPixel data pin. The "BUTTONS" block shows
// SW1 pulled up to 3.3V via R14 (100K) with one contact wired to IO9 and
// the other side to GND - a standard BOOT-button-to-strapping-pin
// wiring, consistent with this board.json's existing pinNotes entry
// "9": "Must be HIGH for normal boot". The same BUTTONS block also shows
// a second switch contact wired to the chip's RESET/EN line (not a
// GPIO), so only IO9 is tagged - the reset button has no user-accessible
// pin to tag.
//
// GPIO23 (RGB_DATA/RGB_BUILTIN): CONFIRMED onboard WS2812 addressable
// RGB LED data pin via vendor schematic. Alias-collision check: this
// board's SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/SDO/SDI/TX/RX aliases are 6/7/18/21/
// 20/19/21/20/16/17 - none equal 23, so no spurious bus capability would
// be appended; no pins_arduino.h edit needed. Tagged capabilities:
// ["digital_output","led_neopixel","pwm_output"], matching this repo's
// led_neopixel precedent (e.g. pandabyte_xc6 GPIO23, esp32c6/esp32c6
// GPIO8).
//
// GPIO9 (BOOT button): CONFIRMED onboard physical BOOT button via vendor
// schematic (SW1/R14, see above). Alias-collision check: GPIO9 is not
// TX/RX/SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK on this board either - no conflict, no
// pins_arduino.h edit needed. Tagged capabilities:
// ["digital_input","button"] only, per this repo's button-pin
// convention (waveshare_esp32_c6_zero GPIO9).
//
// See boardsDetails/esp32/esp32c6/um_tinyc6/notes.txt for the full
// research trail.
